   "summary": "A small first C++ project that converts images into stylized dot matrix images.",
   "description": "This is a small C++ project I did as a way to help introduce myself to the language. The program basically takes a chunk of an image and distills the average value of the pixels and creates a dot with a radius that corresponds to the value. This creates a cool dithered effect that is similar to old comic rendering methods.",
   "learned": "From this project I was able to learn a bit about the basic syntax of C++ and I was able to learn about libraries like SFML and OpenCV and how these can be used to render to the screen and sample from images respectively. I also learned about simple data structures in C++ like vectors and arrays which were useful in storing the modified image data.",
   "takeaway": "While this was a pretty simple project, it definitely brought me some joy programming. I was happy to be able to make something that was actually somewhat interesting despite my low fluency in C++. In the future, I would like to maybe implement this style into some sort of UI that I use but I definitely need more experience before I program UIs…",
