   "summary": "A research and design project that researches the possibility of using machine learning to detect images generated by AI.",
   "description": "For this project I created a chrome extension that could be installed that allows users to check if any image is either an AI image generated by an LLM or a real photo. In order to do this, I also compiled a large data set of open source Real and AI images, and trained my own ML neural network using Microsoft ML. I did this over the span of two years and found that AI Images were becoming harder to detect.",
   "learned": "Through this project I learned how to write in a more formal and scientific way. Additionally, I briefly learned how to use Microsoft ML through Visual Studio to create my neural networks and prediction algorithms. Also, I learned how to create basic chrome extensions that can send and receive data from a web server. Through the research, I learned how to curate and filter through input and output data as well as optimize AI datasets to get predicted results.",
   "takeaway": "This project was a really great introduction for me to better understand how to create and use machine learning techniques in practical ways. I also got a lot of practice for learning how to properly sort and denote data that I collect, and I hope I can take that forward into future AI and machine learning projects that I do…",
