   "summary": "An M&amp;M flinging device made with VEX Robotics parts in combination with a display constructed of cotton, wood, and hot glue.",
   "description": "For this project, I built a large metal contraption out of VEX Robotics parts that had a large motorized arm that catapulted peanut M&amp;Ms many feet away. There were 3 different settings with different power levels, and could be pivoted on the ground to aim. This project was made as a team for the 2024 JPL Invention Challenge. The contraption was covered in decorations, and was supposed to be themed similar to the movie ”Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs”.",
   "learned": "Through this project, I learned a lot about teamwork and how to delegate others to work on certain tasks. I also learned a lot about improvisation, because we accidentally left the parts we had at home, and had to use worse back up parts in order to assemble our design.",
   "takeaway": "This was a really fun project because of the frantic nature of having to assemble with scraps. We also ended up winning 3rd place, as well as the award for art. Despite the win, I was able to take away many lessons about how to make my future projects go more smoothly, and most importantly make sure I bring the parts for what I’m building…",
